<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">North Caucasian Emirate</h1><p class="st-meta">1919 CE – 1920 CE · capital Vedeno</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived Islamic state in Chechnya and Dagestan proclaimed by Sheikh Uzun-Haji in 1919 to fight Denikin's White army.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anton-denikin">Denikin</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volunteer-army">Volunteer Army</a> overran the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mountainous-republic-of-the-northern-caucasus">Mountainous Republic of the Northern Caucasus</a> in 1919, the elderly Naqshbandi sheikh <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzun-haji">Uzun-Haji</a>, who had long called for a revival of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam-shamil">Shamil</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imamate">imamate</a>, proclaimed the North Caucasian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> in September 1919 in the mountains of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chechnya">Chechnya</a>, with its seat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vedeno">Vedeno</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzun-haji">Uzun-Haji</a> ruled as emir under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sharia">sharia</a>, with a government of religious leaders and Ottoman officers, and with a nominal Ottoman sultan as protector. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> formed an army that waged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> war against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-movement">Whites</a> in alliance of convenience with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-party-of-the-soviet-union">Bolsheviks</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>With the defeat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-movement">Whites</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> entered the region in 1920. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzun-haji">Uzun-Haji</a> died in March 1920, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> was dissolved as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Russian SFSR</a> established Soviet rule in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-caucasus">North Caucasus</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/north-caucasian-emirate.jpg" alt="North Caucasian Emirate" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Узун-Хаджи Салтинский · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_North_Caucasian_Emirate.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1919 CE – 1920 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Vedeno</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Uzun-Haji</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Chechen; Avar; Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Emirate of the North Caucasus, Emirate of Uzun-Haji</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1920&amp;focus=north-caucasian-emirate" aria-label="North Caucasian Emirate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5793 652 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where North Caucasian Emirate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6113 908L6078 906M6113 908L5709 970M6113 908L5820 533"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6078 906h0M5709 970h0M5820 533h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6113 908h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6113 908h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Vedeno. <a href="/atlas?year=1920&amp;focus=north-caucasian-emirate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
